# The WebP encoder in this directory, pinned (ADR 0127 decision 2). Written by `build.py --write`, never by hand.
#
# tag     the libwebp release tag it is built from (a stable vX.Y.Z; libwebp publishes tags, no GitHub releases)
# commit  the commit that tag must be, read with `git ls-remote https://github.com/webmproject/libwebp refs/tags/<tag>^{}`
#         when the tag was taken; the build refuses a tag that has moved since
# image   the Emscripten image that compiles it — the Dockerfile's FROM, the same string
# sha256  each output's SHA-256 and its path in this directory
#
# `build.py` rebuilds and compares with these lines and the committed files (CI's rebuild check), and
# scripts/validate_build_input_pins.py holds them together offline: the outputs hash to these lines, and the image
# is the Dockerfile's.
tag v1.6.0
